SUMMARY:Seventh Town Historical Society - British Home Children in Prince Edward County
DESCRIPTION:September 28 is British Home Child day in Canada and Seventh Town Historical Society is hosting a special presentation by Sheila Dodd – an active volunteer\, committee member and\naccredited speaker with Home Children Canada (HCC) since 2019. \nSheila has researched several local area British Home Children (BHC) and has worked with their families to bring their stories to life. She has also served on the Liverpool Monument Committee representing HCC to have a statue placed at Liverpool harbour\, England\, to commemorate the 118\,000 BHC who sailed from Liverpool to Canada. \nGuests must register to attend as space is limited. Visit our online ticket site to register.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/seventh-town-historical-society-british-home-children-in-prince-edward-county/
LOCATION:Marilyn Adams Genealogical Research Centre\, 528 County Road 19\, Ameliasburgh\, K0K 1A0\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Seventh Town Historical Society":MAILTO:info@seventhtownresearch.com
GEO:44.0589032;-77.4368037
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Marilyn Adams Genealogical Research Centre 528 County Road 19 Ameliasburgh K0K 1A0 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=528 County Road 19:geo:-77.4368037,44.0589032
END:VEVENT
